  {
    "sha": "ceac40dd977f9b5fccae5ed31080b2629a501cca",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGNlYWM0MGRkOTc3ZjliNWZjY2FlNWVkMzEwODBiMjYyOWE1MDFjY2E",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T12:39:46Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T12:39:46Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): keep the floor passes of the first band when the split is at its first level\n\nWhen the first band of a whole-model 2D Contour splits at index 0, a ring\ncan still have a floor pass above the first flat level (#2004 floor\nsearch). The fallback re-sliced the region and dropped that pass and its\nring notes, so the wall above was left uncut with no note.\n\nThe band-0 split now trims the ladder at the first level, like the\nSome(j) arm: it emits the trimmed band, forwards the notes, records the\nregion and sets the ceiling before the re-slice.\n\nPins: large_stepdown_keeps_the_upper_island_floor_pass_before_the_plate,\ncounterbore_changing_before_first_cut_level_keeps_lower_bore (Z 10 lap).\n\nRefs #2436\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
