  {
    "sha": "3dd8e343820c1ead96d84f1d259ef1426b321748",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDNkZDhlMzQzODIwYzFlYWQ5NmQ4NGYxZDI1OWVmMTQyNmIzMjE3NDg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T13:05:17Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T13:05:23Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): cut the floor of a middle outline that has no flat level\n\nA whole-model contour band skipped an outline whose Z range held no\nflat level (a middle step between two cut levels). That wall was never\ncut and the result was Ok with no note.\n\nWhen the outline just under the band ceiling differs from the outline at\nthe next flat level, the band loop now runs an intermediate band with its\nown floor pass at that outline. If the intermediate band has no floor\nlevel, the result carries a visible note that names the uncut Z range.\nA loop that stops with levels left now returns an error, not a silent Ok.\n\nThe slice helpers move to contour_whole_slice.rs to keep the file short.\nThe app test gets its Gate map line and the lap-length comments agree.\n\nPinned by middle_step_without_a_flat_level_gets_its_floor_pass.\n\nRefs #2436\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
